Pay Me, chaotic Monk, and powerful Leader of the White Lotus, after having
obtained the AoY, fought a long, hard battle through Gehennom.

The Wizard of Yendor would not relent, stole the Eyes of the Overworld,
summoned an incredible number of creatures, double troubled, stole the
AoY, got send back down with the AoY while trying to run away...

Through all of this, Pay Me persevered and stood his ground. Even after
an ArchLich disintegrated his robe and he had to switch to the CoMR.
(Mistake number 1, costing some 100 max HP and risking Instadeath to
idiotic un-awareness, since it took for the robe to be disintegrated
to point out the fact that maybe those new glasses the Wizard had were,
in fact, Pay Me's).

Undaunted, Pay Me went after the Wizard and recovered the AoY and the
Eyes of the Overworld numerous times (in the end, Rodney had been killed
13 times).

Seeing as how this was not helping him, the Wizard summoned Yeenoghu,
who promptly stole the AoY and the Wizard got the Eyes again.

Pay Me was surrounded by mosnters, and barely made it to the upstairs,
there he rested and thought. Switching =oSD for =oC, Pay Me once again
descended the stairs and fought Yeenoghu and the Wizard and the Wizard
and assorted other evil creatures.

After Yeenoghu was dead and the AoY recovered, Pay Me longed to have the
Eyes of the Overworld back, so he went down again and assaulted the Wizard.

After a short time, Rodney was scared again and summoned Demogorgon. Pay Me
was not amused. A long long fight ensued, with Pay Me retreating up the
stairs numerous times, but after awhile, even Demogorgon was dead.

Exhausted but with AoY and the Eyes recovered, Pay Me arrived at the VotD.
The temple, long since abandoned, was like a safe haven after being thrown
about in the rough seas of Gehennom.

Pay Me sorted his stash and prepared some things for the trip to exit of
the dungeon, where another stash was already waiting.

On the way there, he visited the High Priest and laughed at him, since now
Pay Me would be the Master!

Rodney only showed up again on the Plane of Earth and was dispatched. The
portal quickly found and reached with WoDiggings. On Air it took three
tries to cast levitation. One Air Elemental engulfed Pay Me but didn't cause
serious concerns. Some other Elementals were teleported away and Pay Me
arrived on the Plane of Fire.

The trip to the portal was uneventful, and on Water, substituting a =oL for
the =oSD, the portal reached without incident.

Pay Me had reached the Astral Plane. A quick check with "Detect Monster"
had Pay Me trying for the Altar on the right, thinking it was guarded by
Famine. Death awaited him there (mistake number 2), along with priests and
Angels but he reached the Altar of Shan Lai Ching and cast Charm Monster on
a few of the Dragons there and made his way back to the arrival point, ready
to test the middle Altar. (Mistake number 3, Pestilence guarded that, so why
not go left to Famine...). That proved the end, priests, angels and
Pestilence were hitting Pay Me. Too late he broke a WoTeleport. The Angels
and Priests were gone, but with out any !oFH, burdened from an un-blessed
BoH, and down to about 50 HP, that was the end of Pay Me, chaotic Monk, and
late Leader of the White Lotus.
